<resources>
    <!-- Default screen margins, per the Android Design guidelines. -->
    <dimen name="activity_horizontal_margin">16dp</dimen>
    <dimen name="activity_vertical_margin">16dp</dimen>
    <dimen name="fab_margin">16dp</dimen>

    <!-- UI Text Size -->
    <dimen name="textsize_connection">20dp</dimen>

    <!-- List View Relative -->
    <dimen name="item_arrow_width">26dp</dimen>
    <dimen name="item_arrow_height">44dp</dimen>
    <dimen name="item_min_height">44dp</dimen>
    <dimen name="item_value_size">18sp</dimen>
    <dimen name="item_title_size">18sp</dimen>
    <dimen name="test_log_textsize">17sp</dimen>
    <dimen name="button_widget">200dp</dimen>
    <!-- Flight-screen mini-map edge. The HUD's right-hand column is the tightest space in the
         app: toolbar, exposure block, telemetry and map all share one landscape screen height,
         and the map is the single largest item. This default is sized for SHORT screens (a
         Samsung S21 is ~411dp tall in landscape); values-h440dp gives taller devices the bigger
         map. Shrinking the map rather than the text keeps the readout legible in daylight,
         which is the part that actually has to work in the field. -->
    <!-- ⚠ REDUCED 2026-08-14 to pay for the HUD panels (conformance D4). The two panels add
         4dp of padding at the top and bottom of each, 16dp in total, and this bucket had only
         5dp of slack in the worst case (FAA ceiling visible). Worst case is now:

             paddingTop 60 + EV slider 24 + map 110 + paddingBottom 12 + margins 20
               + 16 x 10 text lines + 2 panels x 8dp padding = 402dp

         against 411dp of screen, so 9dp of slack. The conformance note on the D1 fix
         names exactly this remedy: take the height from flight_map_size, never by re-joining
         the readout lines. **This is arithmetic, not a measurement.** -->
    <!-- ⚠ 148dp, NOT 110dp, since 2026-08-19. This is the COLUMN width, thus it is also the
         width the aircraft's latitude and longitude have to print in. At 110dp the pair wrapped
         onto two lines on the RC Plus 2 (operator). The coordinate line is about 18 characters
         at roughly 6dp each, about 108dp, and the panel adds 8dp of padding on each side — so
         the column needs about 124dp before the pair fits on one line, and 148dp leaves room
         for a third digit of longitude.

         Raising this widens the MAP too, because the map takes the column's width. That is
         accepted here: the RC Plus 2 is 768dp wide and the column costs 152dp of it.
         flight_map_height is deliberately NOT raised with it — the vertical budget above has
         only about 14dp of slack on this device, while width is abundant. -->
    <!-- WARNING BANNER, per device. Specification §4.8 fixes what the banner IS — top-left,
         white bold, severity on the background — and leaves these two numbers to the device
         since 2026-08-19.
         At the specification's 15sp in 380dp the banner covered about a third of the RC Plus
         2's video, because this screen is 768dp wide where the Autel controller is 1024dp
         (operator). 13sp fits the same text in fewer, shorter lines. The width stays 380dp:
         narrowing it does not shrink the banner, it makes it TALLER, and height is what
         covers the picture. -->
    <dimen name="flight_warning_text_size">13sp</dimen>
    <dimen name="flight_warning_max_width">380dp</dimen>

    <dimen name="flight_map_size">148dp</dimen>
    <!-- ⚠ DERIVED, NOT A FREE NUMBER: flight_map_size + the HUD column's paddingEnd, which is
         4dp since 2026-08-19 (it was 14dp, which left a visible gap against the right edge of
         the screen). 148 + 4 = 152. Change this in EVERY bucket whenever either input moves;
         the specification makes it a MUST because it has silently broken twice. -->
    <dimen name="flight_resource_row_margin_end">152dp</dimen>
    <!-- Separate from flight_map_size so a taller screen can carry a taller map
         without a wider HUD column. Equal to the width today, so the map is square
         and nothing moved when this was introduced (conformance D8). -->
    <dimen name="flight_map_height">110dp</dimen>
    <!-- HUD readout size, per bucket. 12sp is what hudText already used, so this
         changed no pixel; it exists so a controller can raise it (conformance D7).
         On a sunlight-readable screen at arm's length 12sp is too small. -->
    <dimen name="flight_readout_text_size">12sp</dimen>
</resources>
